	}}
>
	<p class="cert-verified">Facts on this page were verified against Anthropic's public pages as of {VERIFIED_AS_OF}. Certification programs change; always confirm on Anthropic's official pages.</p>

	<p>
		In March 2026, Anthropic launched its first technical certification: the
		<strong>Claude Certified Architect, Foundations (CCA-F)</strong>. If you have seen the
		name on LinkedIn and wondered what it actually is, whether you can take it, and where
		the real information lives, this page collects the publicly verifiable facts in one place.
	</p>

	<h2>What it is</h2>
	<p>
		Anthropic announced the certification on March 12, 2026 as part of its
		<a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-partner-network">Claude Partner Network</a> launch,
		describing it as "a technical exam for solution architects building production applications
		with Claude." The certification's own page says it "validates that practitioners can make
		informed decisions about tradeoffs when implementing real-world solutions with Claude,"
		across four core technologies: Claude Code, the Claude Agent SDK, the Claude API, and
		Model Context Protocol (MCP).
	</p>
	<p>
		The exam guide published on Anthropic's Academy page describes the exam's format and
		content domains. That guide, together with the certification terms and the exam policy,
		lives on the official exam page, and it is the document to read first.
	</p>

	<h2>Who can take it today</h2>
	<p>
		As of {VERIFIED_AS_OF}, the certification is offered through Anthropic's partner program:
		it launched as available "today for partners," with certifications earned by individual
		people through Anthropic Academy exams. It is not yet generally available to the public.
		Anthropic Academy provides an access request form for those outside a partner
		organization, and Anthropic's announcement says more certifications are planned, with
		network partners getting priority access as they roll out.
	</p>
	<p>
		If that is disappointing, here is the useful reframe: the skills the certification names
		are all publicly teachable today. Anthropic Academy's free, self-paced courses on the
		Claude API, Claude Code, and MCP are open to everyone, and they are excellent.
	</p>

	<h2>What it costs</h2>
	<p>
		The exam page lists a registration fee of $125. Anthropic's partner announcement notes
		that tiered partners receive discounted rates on a first attempt.
	</p>

	<h2>Where the official details live</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><a href="https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-partner-network">The Claude Partner Network announcement</a>, where the certification debuted.</li>
		<li><a href="https://anthropic-partners.skilljar.com/claude-certified-architect-foundations-certification">The official certification page</a> on Anthropic Academy, with the exam guide, terms, and policy documents.</li>
		<li><a href="https://anthropic.skilljar.com/">Anthropic Academy</a>, the free public course catalog and the access request path.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Building the skills in the meantime</h2>
	<p>
		Clawdemy's free
		<a href="/lessons/engineering-agentic-systems/thinking-like-an-architect/lesson/">Engineering Agentic Systems</a>
		track teaches the underlying skills, from agentic architecture and tool design to
		orchestration and reliability, with no signup and no fee.
	</p>

	<hr />

	<p class="cert-disclaimer">
		Clawdemy is an independent educational project. This page and this site are not
		affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Anthropic. Claude and Claude Certified
		Architect are trademarks of Anthropic, PBC. For official certification information and
		registration, see Anthropic Academy.
	</p>

